        } ]
      }, {
        "name" : "Description",
        "value" : "The sequencing instrument will use the information in sample sheet to generate one file for each sample name provided. In most cases, this file will be in FASTQ format. This file is not the final output of the assay but represents raw sequencing data. Each FASTQ file must be aligned to produce final gene counts. The easiest way to align your FASTQs is to use the Aligner function of TempO-SeqR. If this is not feasible, users should utilize the R script provided by BioSpyder. The TempO-SeqR data analysis option can be used to verify data clustering, perform principal component analysis, and verify reproducibility through scatter plots."
      }, {
        "name" : "Hardware"
      } ]
